<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Home Assistant entity as a reference meter, REST, generic.

  Reads the active power at the grid connection point from ONE Home Assistant
  entity (GET /api/states/<entity_id>, long-lived access token), so that
  grd-sgr can judge F1 and F4 against a meter that is only reachable through
  Home Assistant: a cloud-connected inverter or smart meter, for instance.
  Usage: README, section "Reference meter from Home Assistant" (configuration
  values base_uri, token and entity_id; meter point
  ActivePowerAC.ActivePowerACtot).

  The reading is converted to kW from the entity's own unit (W, kW or MW), and
  signed + import / - export ("sign" = -1 for an entity that counts export as
  positive). A state that is not a number ("unavailable", "unknown"), another
  unit, or a value not reported for "max_age_s" seconds is an ERROR, never a
  number: the bench counts a failed reading, it never reads it as zero.

  Independence: an entity of the EMS's own Home Assistant goes through the
  system under test. grd-sgr says so in its report when the meter and the EMS
  share a host.

  Not declared by the SmartGridready association: release Draft, testState None.
-->
<DeviceFrame xmlns="http://www.smartgridready.com/ns/V0/"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.smartgridready.com/ns/V0/ ../../SchemaDatabase/SGr/Product/Product.xsd">
  <deviceName>Home Assistant Entity Power Meter</deviceName>
  <manufacturerName>grd-smartgridready</manufacturerName>
  <specificationOwnerIdentification>0</specificationOwnerIdentification>
  <releaseNotes>
    <state>Draft</state>
    <changeLog>
      <version>1.0.0</version>
      <date>2026-09-26</date>
      <author>grd-smartgridready</author>
      <comment>Grid power from one Home Assistant entity, as the reference meter of F1 and F4</comment>
    </changeLog>
  </releaseNotes>
  <deviceInformation>
    <legibleDescription>
      <textElement>
        <![CDATA[
          <p>Reads the net active power at the grid connection point from one Home Assistant
          entity, through the Home Assistant REST API, and gives it in kW, positive for import.
          Written for grd-smartgridready, to use as the reference meter of its functional tests
          when the meter is only reachable through Home Assistant.</p>
        ]]>
      </textElement>
      <language>en</language>
      <uri>https://github.com/chrohrbach/grd-smartgridready</uri>
    </legibleDescription>
    <legibleDescription>
      <textElement>
        <![CDATA[
          <p>Liest die Netto-Wirkleistung am Netzanschlusspunkt aus einer Home-Assistant-Entität
          über die REST-API von Home Assistant und gibt sie in kW aus, Bezug positiv. Geschrieben
          für grd-smartgridready, als Referenzzähler der Funktionstests, wenn der Zähler nur über
          Home Assistant erreichbar ist.</p>
        ]]>
      </textElement>
      <language>de</language>
      <uri>https://github.com/chrohrbach/grd-smartgridready</uri>
    </legibleDescription>
    <legibleDescription>
      <textElement>
        <![CDATA[
          <p>Lit la puissance active nette au point de raccordement dans une entité Home Assistant,
          par l'API REST de Home Assistant, et la donne en kW, positive au soutirage. Écrite pour
          grd-smartgridready, comme compteur de référence de ses tests fonctionnels quand le
          compteur n'est joignable que par Home Assistant.</p>
        ]]>
      </textElement>
      <language>fr</language>
      <uri>https://github.com/chrohrbach/grd-smartgridready</uri>
    </legibleDescription>
    <deviceCategory>Generic</deviceCategory>
    <isLocalControl>true</isLocalControl>
    <softwareRevision>1.0</softwareRevision>
    <manufacturerSpecificationIdentification>home-assistant-entity-meter</manufacturerSpecificationIdentification>
    <levelOfOperation>m</levelOfOperation>
    <versionNumber>
      <primaryVersionNumber>1</primaryVersionNumber>
      <secondaryVersionNumber>0</secondaryVersionNumber>
      <subReleaseVersionNumber>0</subReleaseVersionNumber>
    </versionNumber>
    <testState>None</testState>
    <programmerHints>
      <textElement>
        <![CDATA[
          <p>Authentication: a Home Assistant long-lived access token (configuration value
          <i>token</i>), sent as "Authorization: Bearer" on each read. The token is created by the
          owner of the Home Assistant instance (Profile, Security) and can be revoked there; give it
          to grd-sgr through an environment variable (token=env:NAME) so that it is masked in every
          output.</p>
          <p>The response query is a JSONata expression, because sgr-commhandler applies
          neither unitConversionMultiplicator nor value mappings after a query: the expression
          itself converts W, kW or MW to kW, applies <i>sign</i>, and raises an error for a state
          that is not a number, for any other unit, and for a value last reported more than
          <i>max_age_s</i> seconds ago (last_reported, or last_updated on Home Assistant before
          2024.3). A frozen cloud feed therefore fails the reading instead of feeding a
          plausible value to a verdict.</p>
          <p>Read-only: the profile has no write call.</p>
        ]]>
      </textElement>
      <language>en</language>
    </programmerHints>
  </deviceInformation>
  <configurationList>
    <configurationListElement>
      <name>base_uri</name>
      <dataType>
        <string />
      </dataType>
      <defaultValue>http://homeassistant.local:8123</defaultValue>
      <configurationDescription>
        <textElement>Base address of Home Assistant, without /api</textElement>
        <language>en</language>
        <label>Base URI</label>
      </configurationDescription>
    </configurationListElement>
    <configurationListElement>
      <name>token</name>
      <dataType>
        <string />
      </dataType>
      <configurationDescription>
        <textElement>Home Assistant long-lived access token</textElement>
        <language>en</language>
        <label>Access token</label>
      </configurationDescription>
    </configurationListElement>
    <configurationListElement>
      <name>entity_id</name>
      <dataType>
        <string />
      </dataType>
      <configurationDescription>
        <textElement>Entity giving the power at the grid connection point, in W, kW or MW (for example sensor.grid_power)</textElement>
        <language>en</language>
        <label>Entity</label>
      </configurationDescription>
    </configurationListElement>
    <configurationListElement>
      <name>sign</name>
      <dataType>
        <int32 />
      </dataType>
      <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
      <configurationDescription>
        <textElement>1 if the entity counts import as positive, -1 if it counts export as positive</textElement>
        <language>en</language>
        <label>Sign</label>
      </configurationDescription>
    </configurationListElement>
    <configurationListElement>
      <name>max_age_s</name>
      <dataType>
        <int32 />
      </dataType>
      <defaultValue>300</defaultValue>
      <configurationDescription>
        <textElement>Oldest accepted value, seconds since Home Assistant last received it</textElement>
        <language>en</language>
        <label>Maximum age</label>
      </configurationDescription>
    </configurationListElement>
    <configurationListElement>
      <name>verify_certificate</name>
      <dataType>
        <string />
      </dataType>
      <defaultValue>true</defaultValue>
      <configurationDescription>
        <textElement>false to accept a self-signed HTTPS certificate</textElement>
        <language>en</language>
        <label>Verify certificate</label>
      </configurationDescription>
    </configurationListElement>
  </configurationList>
  <interfaceList>
    <restApiInterface>
      <restApiInterfaceDescription>
        <restApiInterfaceSelection>URI</restApiInterfaceSelection>
        <restApiUri>{{base_uri}}</restApiUri>
        <restApiAuthenticationMethod>NoSecurityScheme</restApiAuthenticationMethod>
        <restApiVerifyCertificate>{{verify_certificate}}</restApiVerifyCertificate>
      </restApiInterfaceDescription>
      <functionalProfileList>
        <functionalProfileListElement>
          <functionalProfile>
            <functionalProfileName>ActivePowerAC</functionalProfileName>
            <functionalProfileIdentification>
              <specificationOwnerIdentification>0</specificationOwnerIdentification>
              <functionalProfileCategory>Metering</functionalProfileCategory>
              <functionalProfileType>ActivePowerAC</functionalProfileType>
              <levelOfOperation>m</levelOfOperation>
              <versionNumber>
                <primaryVersionNumber>1</primaryVersionNumber>
                <secondaryVersionNumber>1</secondaryVersionNumber>
                <subReleaseVersionNumber>0</subReleaseVersionNumber>
              </versionNumber>
            </functionalProfileIdentification>
          </functionalProfile>
          <genericAttributeList>
            <genericAttributeListElement>
              <name>MeteringDirection</name>
              <dataType>
                <enum>
                  <enumEntry>
                    <literal>Net</literal>
                  </enumEntry>
                  <enumEntry>
                    <literal>Import</literal>
                  </enumEntry>
                  <enumEntry>
                    <literal>Export</literal>
                  </enumEntry>
                </enum>
              </dataType>
              <value>Net</value>
              <unit>NONE</unit>
            </genericAttributeListElement>
            <genericAttributeListElement>
              <name>MeteringTariffNr</name>
              <dataType>
                <int32 />
              </dataType>
              <value>0</value>
              <unit>NONE</unit>
            </genericAttributeListElement>
          </genericAttributeList>
          <dataPointList>
            <dataPointListElement>
              <dataPoint>
                <dataPointName>ActivePowerACtot</dataPointName>
                <dataDirection>R</dataDirection>
                <dataType>
                  <float64 />
                </dataType>
                <unit>KILOWATTS</unit>
                <legibleDescription>
                  <textElement>Net active power at the grid connection point (+ import, - export), from the Home Assistant entity {{entity_id}}</textElement>
                  <language>en</language>
                </legibleDescription>
              </dataPoint>
              <restApiDataPointConfiguration>
                <dataType>JSON_number</dataType>
                <restApiReadServiceCall>
                  <requestHeader>
                    <header>
                      <headerName>Accept</headerName>
                      <value>application/json</value>
                    </header>
                    <header>
                      <headerName>Authorization</headerName>
                      <value>Bearer {{token}}</value>
                    </header>
                  </requestHeader>
                  <requestMethod>GET</requestMethod>
                  <requestPath>/api/states/{{entity_id}}</requestPath>
                  <responseQuery>
                    <queryType>JSONataExpression</queryType>
                    <query><![CDATA[(
  $unit := attributes.unit_of_measurement;
  $factor := $unit = "W" ? 0.001 : $unit = "kW" ? 1 : $unit = "MW" ? 1000
    : $error("{{entity_id}}: unit " & $string($unit) & " is not W, kW or MW");
  $seen := last_reported ? last_reported : last_updated;
  $age := ($millis() - $toMillis($seen)) / 1000;
  $age > {{max_age_s}} ? $error("{{entity_id}}: stale, last reported " & $string($round($age)) & " s ago");
  $number(state) * $factor * {{sign}}
)]]></query>
                  </responseQuery>
                </restApiReadServiceCall>
              </restApiDataPointConfiguration>
            </dataPointListElement>
          </dataPointList>
        </functionalProfileListElement>
      </functionalProfileList>
    </restApiInterface>
  </interfaceList>
</DeviceFrame>
